**.idea/**
**.vscode/**
**/__pycache__/**
secrets.ini
secrets.local.ini

# Claude Code: ignore local/personal config, but track the project-shared harness.
# settings.local.json stays ignored on purpose — it is the personal-override file.
#
# Read the negations carefully, they are not uniform:
#   !.claude/settings.json  un-ignores ONE file.
#   !.claude/skills/  and  !.claude/hooks/  un-ignore WHOLE SUBTREES — anything
#   dropped in either directory becomes committable to a PUBLIC repo with no
#   further gitignore backstop. If a hook ever writes a log, a cache, or a token
#   beside itself, add an explicit re-ignore below, as done for __pycache__.
# Everything under .claude/ NOT reached by a negation stays ignored via `.claude/*`.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/__pycache__/
tmpclaude-*

# Log files
*.log
data/*.log

# Local data files (timestamped copies - CI manages these)
data/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_*.json
data/market_proxy_cache.json
data/backtest_quality_report.json

# Test coverage
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
*.cover
.hypothesis/
